      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Harrisville%2C_Wisconsin"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Early economic growth in Harrisville was driven by the Montello River, which provided water power for local mills and factories.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/harrisville_wisconsin"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Harris Pond is a 172-acre body of water in Harrisville that provides public boat access for local recreation and fishing.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
